{"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODY0NDM5","login":"AJ0070","name":"Jash Ambaliya","databaseId":87864439}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","is_bot":false,"login":"Krastanov","name":"Stefan Krastanov"},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `LEMON` wrapper [$400]\n\nThe JuliaGraphs/LEMONGraphs.jl package already exists and provides an extremely barebones wrapper for the LEMON C++ library. It is barely more than a proof of concept for the build infrastructure. A lot of this work probably will not be directly in the Graphs.jl repository.\n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the C++ structures of LEMON (slow converters already exist for simple graphs)\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the LEMONGraph types (so that LEMONGraph types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to LEMON implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in LEMONGraphs `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::LEMONAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the C++ implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to LEMONGraph if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in LEMON that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that LEMONGraphs is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the CxxWrap interface package.\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh8669UYo","author":{"login":"MAVRICK-1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Krastanov can i work on this issue ","createdAt":"2025-07-30T14:35:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3136636456","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh8669qx5","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Hi, @MAVRICK-1 ! Could you share any background you might have in Julia or C++, and in what steps you would like to solve this bounty? If you are familiar with the languages and have some rough plan, I would be happy to assign the bounty to you.","createdAt":"2025-07-30T14:57:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3136728185","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh866-LFx","author":{"login":"MAVRICK-1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Krastanov i have knowledge about juila current i am working on this pr https://github.com/JuliaEarth/GeoIO.jl/pull/172","createdAt":"2025-07-30T15:35:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3136860529","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh866-Qve","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Great! Could you answer the rest of my questions: C++ experience, plans of how to tackle this bounty, etc.","createdAt":"2025-07-30T15:42:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3136883678","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh866-bq6","author":{"login":"MAVRICK-1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Krastanov \n  i have Experience with C++/other language bindings and cross-language interop sand  Familiar with memory management and performance optimization\n\n  ### Solution Plan\n\n  Core Strategy: Build fast, memory-safe conversion layer between Graphs.jl\n   and LEMON C++ structures using CxxWrap.jl\n\n  Implementation:\n  - Create robust type mappings between Julia and LEMON graph structures\n  - Implement complete Graphs.jl API for LEMONGraph types\n  - Expose LEMON's unique algorithms (network flows, matching) with clean\n  Julia interfaces\n  - Add dispatch methods for GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim integration\n\n  Quality Assurance:\n  - Use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl for API compliance testing\n  - Comprehensive test suite and documentation\n  - Performance profiling at Julia/C++ boundaries\n\n  The goal is a production-ready wrapper that gives Julia access to LEMON's\n   powerful graph algorithms while maintaining performance and API\n  consistency with the existing Graphs.jl ecosystem.\n","createdAt":"2025-07-30T15:55:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3136928442","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh866_HHF","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Thanks, @MAVRICK-1 ! I will proceed with assigning the bounty to you. Please make sure that:\n\n- you submit small PRs -- one big large PR will probably never get reviewed, but multiple small ones will be easy to review. Do not lump disparate changes in the same PR.\n- make sure you rely on the existing LEMON wrapper and extend it, instead of reimplementing things from scratch\n- if you use any LLM tools, make sure to disclose their use in the PR description","createdAt":"2025-07-30T16:44:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3137106373","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-Yg4C","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Hi, @MAVRICK-1 ! Just wanted to double check whether you are still working on this bounty? There is no rush on it, you have plenty of time to work on it, I just wanted to make sure you are still interested. I am asking because we have not had a discussion after I left a few comments on your PR.","createdAt":"2025-08-17T03:27:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"off-topic","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3194097154","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-YhBW","author":{"login":"MAVRICK-1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Krastanov currently I am learning a few things to implement it more better ","createdAt":"2025-08-17T03:29:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3194097750","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87DtuiR","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Hi, @MAVRICK-1 ! How is this going? Is there anything I can help with?","createdAt":"2025-09-12T03:45:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3283544209","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87dsNFH","author":{"login":"jph6366"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi @Krastanov, is this open for contribution? \n\nMy current background in Julia has been learning the language starting early last year and also contributing to GeoIO.jl https://github.com/JuliaEarth/GeoIO.jl/pull/188\nI also have spent some time last year working with Flux.jl,  and other Julia packages for statistics, data science, and genAI\n\nIn C++ I worked with the Point Cloud Library (PCL) in my previous job as SWE, and I have written C++ using _Kitware_'s Visualization Toolkit (VTK) and CMake. ( an older repo I wrote for practice https://github.com/jph6366/Surf-Seg)\nI have been following this on-going lecture series [Master's Course in C++](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL3BR09unfgcjSJXcCn7Y6VBdGfyqeix5w).\n\nIf this PR is open to be reassigned, then I shall work on writing up a fresh implementation plan before starting up a new initiative.\n\n","createdAt":"2026-01-07T15:16:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3719352647","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87dt-sS","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@jph6366 , please feel free to give it a try. Please aim to submit small PRs, ton one large one -- that helps a lot with review. Starting with things focused on tests would also be easier.","createdAt":"2026-01-07T16:56:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3719818002","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oKEek","author":{"login":"zhanglin2603"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I reviewed JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl#447 and I'm ready to handle it (listed bounty: $400).\n- My read: this is primarily a UI/UX task tied to \"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C++ library `LEMON` [$400]\".\n- I will focus on these issue-specific points first: reliable, idiomatic, wrapper.\n- First I will reproduce and confirm expected behavior for the UI/UX path.\n- Then I will implement the fix with targeted tests and keep scope tight (good confidence).\n- I will share a working PR update fast (24h for scoped implementation plan, 48h+ for full patch and validation) with verification notes.\nIf this approach works for you, I can start now.\n","createdAt":"2026-02-13T05:18:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3894953892","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oK2JY","author":{"login":"lmee"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I reviewed \"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C++ library `LEMON` [$400]\" end-to-end and read all thread comments. The core problem appears to be: A reliable idiomatic wrapper [$400]. My root-cause hypothesis is an FFI boundary mismatch (types/ownership/error handling) between wrapper code and native APIs. A key detail from the discussion is: \"@Krastanov i have Experience with C++/other language bindings and cross-language interop sand Familiar with memory management and performance optimization Solution Plan Core Strate.\" My plan is to define a minimal wrapper surface first, align types and ownership semantics with the native API, then add deterministic tests for correctness, memory safety, and failure-path behavior. I can start right away and keep the first patch scoped for fast review. Best, Jerry Li","createdAt":"2026-02-13T06:28:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3895157336","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87olkE3","author":{"login":"jph6366"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Ive logged time reading through and typing out (for rote memorization) JuliaGraphs documentation and most of LEMON's documentation. you can see my [monolith of notes [on implementing LEMONGraphs.jl]](https://jph6366.github.io/filing-cabinet/TOP-DOWN/Kanban/LEMONGraphs.html) at my personal site for note-taking. for reviewing and tracking important details concerning the completion of this issue/bounty.\n\nAlso I've got my local dev setup with LEMON installed and a testing pipeline to locally test changes made to `lemoncxxwrap.cpp` and build the binaries for testing downstream in `LEMONGraphs.jl` using julia code.\n\n_I had Claude Sonnet help scope this PR given my monolith `.org` file notes._\n\n**I won't be following this exactly but just to help getting started for now**\n\n- Once my setup is clean, I'll be able launch into my environment and be able to focus on code quality and trajectory of consecutive and sequential PRs\n\nBelow is shortened response of the entire generated markdown file detailing the scope of the issue.\n\n> This roadmap provides a structured approach to implementing LEMONGraphs.jl through 43 focused PRs across 9 phases. Each PR is scoped to be reviewable (typically < 500 lines), tested comprehensively, and documented clearly. The phased approach allows for early feedback and iterative improvement while building toward the complete feature set outlined in the project requirements.\n\n> \n> PR #1 (Conversions) ──┬─► PR #2 (AbstractGraph API) ──┬─► Most other PRs\n>                       │                                │\n>                       └─► PR #4 (Maps) ◄──────────────┘\n>                                 │\n>                                 ├─► PR #11 (Dijkstra)\n>                                 ├─► PR #28 (MST)\n>                                 └─► PR #30 (Flow)\n> \n> PR #6 (BFS) ──┬─► PR #17 (Connectivity)\n>               └─► PR #18 (Bipartiteness)\n> \n> PR #7 (DFS) ──┬─► PR #19 (Articulation)\n>               └─► PR #20 (Cycles)\n> \n> PR #11 (Dijkstra) ──┬─► PR #13 (A*)\n>                     ├─► PR #34 (Centrality)\n>                     └─► PR #36 (Distance)\n> \n> All Algorithm PRs ──► PR #37 (Algorithm Discovery)\n\nI'm also happy to help review and debug other smaller PRs contributed by commentors above.","createdAt":"2026-02-14T16:48:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3902161207","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87pB0D7","author":{"login":"energypantry"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi @Krastanov, I read the full thread and noticed this is currently tagged `bounty:reserved`.\n\nIf there is still room for another contributor (or if the reservation is stale), I can start with a tightly-scoped PR sequence:\n- conversion/view layer from `Graphs.jl` types to `LEMONGraphs.jl`,\n- a small set of benchmarkable algorithms,\n- tests + docs in separate review-friendly commits.\n\nI will keep PRs small and compartmentalized per your review guidance. Please let me know whether this thread is still open for a fresh claim.\n","createdAt":"2026-02-16T16:57:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-3909566715","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAP5kRA","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov Is this still open? I have prior experience in C++ (I’ve done a lot of competitive programming and DSA) and Julia (I’ve been working in the SciML ecosystem for a while and have also completed [a bounty there](https://sciml.ai/small_grants/#add_sympyjl_as_an_alternative_backend_for_symbolicsjl_300)), and I would like to take a shot at this.","createdAt":"2026-04-24T08:08:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-4311639108","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABARVrqQ","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Hi, @AJ0070 -- it is indeed unfinished and in need of work, but I think @jph6366 has currently claimed it. There has also been a bunch of LLM spam from bot accounts (or human accounts submitting purely LLM generated PRs elsewhere), I will go ahead and clean that up.\n\nGiven that is has been claimed for quite a few months now, let's wait a couple of days for an answer by @jph6366 in case they are still working on it (no worries if not, it is perfectly reasonable for a volunteer contributor to switch focus midway through something and to forget about an initial assignment -- I have done that myself plenty).","createdAt":"2026-04-24T12:29:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-4313148329","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAXxdWA","author":{"login":"jph6366"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I wanted to circle back to working on the project, but I have been booked up with work upon new hiring for internship role, **so I encourage someone else to start it up**. And I can try to follow along to see how it going to be curated. But it is indeed sitting on my todo list to find the best route for high-performance through LEMON.cpp's available interfaces.","createdAt":"2026-04-25T14:58:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-4319894872","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAX0ECw","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov with the positive response from @jph6366 I am going to start work on this as soon as possible.","createdAt":"2026-04-25T15:20:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-4319937547","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAZbfyA","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov I’ll first open a Yggdrasil PR with extended CxxWrap bindings in `lemoncxxwrap.cpp`, including additional graph accessors/maps and Dijkstra bindings.\n\nAfter that, I’ll open a PR in LEMONGraphs to enable those bindings, and then add API stubs and documentation in Graph.jl.\n","createdAt":"2026-04-26T08:32:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447#issuecomment-4321632200","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2025-07-24T19:27:37Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","name":"bounty","description":"There is an award for solving this issue.","color":"A6D60A"},{"id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","name":"bounty:400","description":"","color":"aaaaaa"},{"id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGiRRwA","name":"bounty:reserved","description":"","color":"aaaaaa"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C++ library `LEMON` [$400]","updatedAt":"2026-04-26T23:47:50Z","url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447"}
